    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**`OwnerDerivations.java`**\n- Redesigned `identityKey(telephone, email, lastName)` to return `SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))` \u2014 a 64-char lowercase hex string (was the plaintext `tel|email|householdId`).\n- Added a correct American **Soundex** implementation (`soundex` + `soundexDigit`), including the `h`/`w` and vowel-separation rules (e.g. `Ashcraft \u2192 A261`).\n\n**`Owner.java`**\n- `getIdentityKey()` now feeds `lastName` (not `householdId`) into the derivation.\n- Added a `public static String soundex(String)` helper so the controller shares one algorithm.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Added `isDuplicateIdentity(owner)` and a **409 Conflict** in `createNewOwner` when the identity key matches an existing **non-deleted** owner (`activeOwners()` filters deleted). The email-domain blocklist still runs first (in `normalizeNewOwner`, before this check).\n- Rewrote `isSoftMatch`: now triggers when **identity keys differ** but `soundex(lastName)` and `postcode` match \u2014 so two owners with the same last name + postcode but **different telephones** are created as a soft match, not rejected.\n- Removed reliance on the old household-based hard-duplicate path; duplicate detection is now solely the identity key.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**\n- Updated `identityKey`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, and the write-only `sharesHousehold` descriptions/examples to match the new behaviour.\n\nBoth existing/new acceptance tests pass: `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` (verifies the `[0-9a-f]{64}` shape) and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` (identical telephone/email/lastName \u2192 409).",
